    <string name="privacy_policy">Privacy policy</string>
    <!-- The body of PRIVACY.md; PrivacyPolicyTest compares them. -->
    <string name="privacy_policy_text">motoLauncher collects no personal data and shares none. It has no accounts, advertising, analytics or tracking.\n\nEverything the launcher stores — favourites, links, hidden apps, settings, and the park lock PIN, which is kept only as a salted hash — stays in its private storage on the device. If Android backup is switched on, Android may include these settings in the device backup.\n\nThe list of installed apps is read only to show and launch them.\n\nWith the GPS speed display switched on, the launcher reads the device location while the home screen is visible, to show the current speed. The location is neither recorded nor sent anywhere.\n\nThe status bar reads the Wi-Fi signal strength and, with the cellular indicator switched on, the mobile signal strength, to draw its signal bars.\n\nThe Google Play version makes no network connections. The version from the GitHub release page connects to GitHub only when you tap the update check, to look for and download a newer version.\n\nQuestions: https://github.com/c0dev0id/motoLauncher/issues</string>
